:: Himari - Errand Boy [bg-sanctuary]
<h1 class="ptitle">NEGAN'S OFFICE</h1>
<<run setup.himari.mark('errand')>>
<<addmins 30>>
<br />
Negan had his boots on the desk and a map spread across his knees that he was not reading. He waved you to the chair across from him and did not offer you a drink, which on this ship meant business.
<br /><br />
<<negan>>
	Here's my problem. I've got two hundred men on this ship. Every one of them has two hands and a dick and about a teaspoon of sense, and after yesterday I've got one less hand and the same amount of sense.
<</negan>>
<br />
He folded the map and dropped it on the floor.
<br /><br />
<<negan>>
	I can't trust a single one of them around her. You, on the other hand... You've got a car. You've got your own little place out there somewhere, which I do not care about. And you've got nothing to gain by being stupid. So, congratulations. You're her handler.
<</negan>>
<br />
He took a small brass key and a padlock on a loop of wire off a nail behind the desk, and dropped them in front of you.
<br /><br />
<center>
	<<image 'people/himari/errand_key.jpg'>>
</center>
<br />
<<negan>>
	Water. Food. The doc, when the doc wants her. The bucket. She doesn't leave that box unless I say so. You open it, you do your job, and you lock it again when you're done. Twenty caps a day for your trouble. And you keep your hands to yourself, because you saw what happens.
<</negan>>
<br />
He leaned forward and his voice dropped, friendly, almost kind.
<br /><br />
<<negan>>
	And kid? Don't get attached. She's not a stray cat you found in the rain. She's a delivery. Deliveries leave.
<</negan>>
<br />
It was not a question, and he did not wait for an answer. He was already reaching for the bottle when you picked up the key.
<br /><br />
<strong>(The container is now in the Sanctuary menu. You can talk to her, teach her words, bring her food and do your handler rounds for <<= setup.himari.JOB_PAY>> caps a day. Negan's people will notice every kindness.)</strong>
<br /><br />
<<link 'Leave'>>
	<<goto 'Sanctuary'>>
<</link>>
